# Task 16 - Selecting Rows and Columns with loc and iloc

## Overview
This project demonstrates how to select rows and columns from a Pandas DataFrame using loc[] and iloc[].

## What I Practiced
- Creating a Pandas DataFrame
- Selecting a single row using loc[]
- Selecting multiple rows using loc[]
- Selecting single and multiple columns using loc[]
- Filtering rows using loc[]
- Selecting rows using iloc[]
- Selecting single and multiple columns using iloc[]
- Selecting specific rows and columns using iloc[]
- Comparing loc[] and iloc[]

## Tools Used
- Python
- Pandas
- Jupyter Notebook

## Outcome
This task helped me understand how to select specific rows and columns from a DataFrame using labels and integer positions.

## Files
- `task16_pandas_loc_iloc.ipynb` - Notebook containing code examples and outputs.